it  is the beginning of november 2020 and  it's already kicking off to  quite a tense month because of the  election stuff  so i'm gonna take a little break and  we're going to do our monthly  update video in which i'll talk about  what went on in october  quite a lot and what we've got coming up  in november  which is a little bit less but also  still  quite a lot of interesting stuff so  i always like to begin by talking about  three big things  big thing number one is october was you  know a major month for everything  stoicism related  i was in several different stoic stoicon  x's as well as organizing the stoic on x  midwest so there's a lot of videos that  i'm linking to below  that you can watch from all of those  events  big thing number two we've got coming up  this month  at the very end of the month we're going  to be going back into ursula k le guin's  earth sea but now we're going beyond the  trilogy to the next  three books in the series that rounded  out  and and really add a lot to that world  big thing number three  we've got our classic metal class coming  up a little bit later this month  and this time we are going to be talking  about the new wave of british heavy  metal  one of the really major movements that  that put it  on you know the genre back on the map  you could say so i hope you can join me  for that classic metal class uh in two  saturdays  okay so what went on in the month of  october  as i mentioned there was a lot of stoic  related stuff we had stoic  week we had uh the main stoic con  i actually spoke at two different  stoicon x's in addition to organizing  the big stoicon x midwest here  you know cited in milwaukee but covering  all those places there's videos  you can watch of all those down below i  also did  along with scott truly my collaborator  the classic metal class and we tackled  an interesting ethical  problem that arises about the ethics of  doing farewell tours and it not being a  farewell tour  i did my normal ama that's ask me  anything session i also did a  political theory and practice discussion  focused on  what stoicism has to tell us about  politics  and then i did my usual you know hegel q  a and discussion sessions both the  public one and the  one for patreon supporters we had uh  our you know worlds of speculative  fiction  series ongoing events with focusing on  ursula k leguins  earth c trilogy which of course expanded  to be six books later on we only focused  on the  first three and we had a really great  wisdom for life  radio show session we weren't able to  get as many in as we normally do  in part because of illness on the part  of myself and  my co-host but we did have one session  where we had a special guest  michael devito a former defensive  lineman coming in we discussed rational  sportsmanship and fandom and stuff like  that so  that that's well worth checking out as  well this is a very busy part of the  semester as far as classes go  midterms you know students panicking  about  how they're doing or how they're not  doing being told by their advisors to  get in touch with all of their  professors  lots and lots of content developed on my  part i probably shot over a hundred  course videos for between  world religions biomedical ethics  business ethics and a few things for the  existentialism class  i also did shoot a lot of other videos  so there's the event videos that you can  check out  but there were also uh core concept  videos on miguel de uno numo  lev or leo shestoff and franz kafka  did an unboxing video about you know  stuff for  our cat sassy and i did a few answers to  common questions videos  and a at least one saddler's stories i'm  not sure if i did  one or two of those podcasting  some of you may have been following on  my soundcloud you know  what what's been recently there we've we  started the month with releasing the  last of the aj air  content language truth and logic then we  jumped into augustine for  most of the month and did stuff coming  from  city of god and from on free choice of  the will  and then we've been releasing stuff on  jon stewart mills utilitarianism over  about the last week or so so that's  what's been going on  this last what we've got coming up  we have quite a few events coming up in  november not quite so much  as in october and i frankly i need to  take a bit of a break between  uh you know the grueling teaching  schedule the  election all the stoic related stuff  and you know doing all this while being  sick from time to time um you know i i'm  really looking forward to thanksgiving  break  so we're gonna start out with a lot of  events  in the early part of the month and then  as we get towards the later part of the  month we have a few less  the very first saturday uh that's  saturday the the seventh  at 12 p.m ama session ask me anything  you can come in and ask me all sorts of  questions and i'll respond to them  on the seventh as well we're going to  have our philosophy chat for patreon  supporters  that's a perk for people who support at  a certain level that'll be at 2 p.m  and then at 4 p.m another wisdom for  life  episode you know you can listen to  wisdom for life 4 p.m  central every saturday it may be a new  episode or it may be a replay of an  older episode depending on what dan and  my schedule  looks like but we are recording  something new responding to  all the election stuff so if you're  interested in that you might want to  check that out we'll also be talking  about like how to  keep yourself sane during this time  then uh the next day at uh the the  eighth that is  at 12 p.m i'll have my political theory  and practice discussion i will be  talking about what to make  of of this election and i'll do a little  bit of a presentation and then i take  you know audience questions and comments  and  address and answer those on the 10th  at 6 p.m we have our milwaukee sofia  meeting this is open  because we're online to people outside  of milwaukee of course we've had people  coming  as far away as brazil and we're going to  be talking about resilience which may  also be useful  given the results of the election  on the 11th at 5 pm i'll be having my  my public hegel q a and discussion  that's you know underwritten by my  patreon supporters but you don't have to  be a patreon supporter to show up and  talk about hegel german idealism  philosophy  i do that as sort of a public service on  the  14th that's the second saturday at  12 p.m scott taruli and i will be  having our next session of the classic  medal class and we're going to be  talking about  we'll probably devote more than one  session to this we're gonna be talking  about the  new wave of british heavy metal so if  you aren't familiar with it that's bands  like  iron maiden saxon diamond head  venom raven all these great bands that  were so  massively influential and we're gonna  we're gonna talk quite a bit about that  um then on the 19th i'm not quite sure  if we're going to be doing anything for  sophia that depends on my co-organizers  but it is world philosophy day so  there's  probably going to be something  interesting going on i might do a little  you know  event of my own you know just get on  youtube and  and let people ask questions on saturday  the 28th we're going to have  two events going on so earlier in the  day  we'll have at 12 o'clock and at 1  30 the world's a speculative fiction  series discussion now i give you two  times for that because the  first time is actually a video premiere  of me  you know discussing the ins and outs of  books five four five and six of the  earthsea  series and you can engage in live chat  and i'll you know  chat back with you on that as you're  watching that video for the very first  time you can be the first people to  watch it  and to comment on it then at 1 30 we  have a zoom discussion so  video conferencing much more intimate  that's for people who want to have you  know  more discussion about these these great  novels and short stories that that she  created in the whole world  then a little bit later that day on the  28th  at 6 pm we'll be having the milwaukee  stoic fellowship  monthly meeting which we're discussing  antonio maccaro's great book on buddhism  and  and stoicism you don't have to be from  milwaukee to join us with that again we  have people from all over  the place who because we're online join  up with us  and that is going to be uh quite  interesting  as well so that finishes out the month's  events  what do we have going on in terms of  videos well i still have one more kafka  video to release i'm going to be  releasing some  some videos on marcel that's gabriel  marcel  and his on the ontological mystery i  shot some new videos from my  existentialism class  i have to shoot some videos on simone de  bevoir on the ethics of ambiguity so  you'll see those coming out  and then i'm hoping to get to the the  videos on albert camus  i have some more stuff on myth sisyphus  to shoot as well  i'll also be doing you know the  personally oriented sadler stories  i'll do some more of the answers to  common questions about stoicism  hoping to get some half hour hegel  videos shot now that things are starting  to settle down  a bit as far as the semester goes and  we've got a nice break coming up  and uh some book review videos i'm i'm  really behind on book reviews and i'm  going to be shooting some of those  as well and then finally you know there  will be videos from the various events  like the classic metal class the  earthsea as i mentioned  and of course the ama and political  theory and discussion  as far as the podcast goes i've still  got some mill utilitarianism  stuff to release after that i will  probably be working on some de bevoir  things from the second sex  and i also have some some stuff from  hegel the self-consciousness section  that i'd like to turn into podcasts  as well so that is what is going on the  rest  of this month of november  going to be you know pretty busy month  but also a time to start  winding down as we get closer to the end  of the year so i hope you can join me at  some of these events  you

